From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt76x02: keep the station power save state across a restart

mt76x02_reset_state() clears the private data of every station before a
full restart, MT_WCID_FLAG_PS included, and mt76x02_sta_add() clears it
again when mac80211 adds the station back. mac80211 keeps
WLAN_STA_PS_STA across the restart, so a station that was asleep is
still in power save for mac80211 but awake for the driver.
mt76_check_sta() reports a power save change only when the PM bit of a
frame differs from MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, so the station's next frames with PM
cleared are not reported, and mac80211 keeps buffering its frames until
the station goes to sleep and wakes up again.

Keep MT_WCID_FLAG_PS across the restart and, on MMIO, set the WCID drop
bit again, as mt76x02_sta_ps() had left them.

Tests of the power save preservation logic on an MT7612E AP used 36
forced restarts with an idle sleeping client. The first post-restart
sample showed mac80211 in power save with the drop bit clear in 0/18
restarts with preservation and 12/18 without it. The drop bit is only
a proxy for the driver flag. These observations support state consistency,
not a demonstrated improvement in packet delivery latency.

Fixes: 004960423fe1 ("mt76: mt76x2: implement full device restart on watchdog reset")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
The hardware observations above used the earlier PS-preservation revision.
They are not a new hardware validation of the revised station-add error
path or of the complete series with the TX-flush ordering change.

--- a/mt76x02_mmio.c
+++ b/mt76x02_mmio.c
@@ -431,6 +431,7 @@
 		struct mt76x02_sta *msta;
 		struct mt76_wcid *wcid;
 		void *priv;
+		bool ps;
 
 		wcid = rcu_dereference_protected(dev->mt76.wcid[i],
 					lockdep_is_held(&dev->mt76.mutex));
@@ -445,8 +446,15 @@
 		priv = msta->vif;
 		vif = container_of(priv, struct ieee80211_vif, drv_priv);
 
+		ps = test_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &wcid->flags);
 		__mt76_sta_remove(&dev->mphy, vif, sta);
 		memset(msta, 0, sizeof(*msta));
+
+		/* mac80211 keeps the station in power save across the
+		 * restart, so mt76x02_sta_add() must restore it as well.
+		 */
+		if (ps)
+			set_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &msta->wcid.flags);
 	}
 
 	dev->mt76.vif_mask = 0;
--- a/mt76x02_util.c
+++ b/mt76x02_util.c
@@ -241,9 +241,15 @@
 	struct mt76x02_dev *dev = container_of(mdev, struct mt76x02_dev, mt76);
 	struct mt76x02_sta *msta = (struct mt76x02_sta *)sta->drv_priv;
 	struct mt76x02_vif *mvif = (struct mt76x02_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
+	/* mac80211 keeps the power save state of a station it adds back, as
+	 * after a restart, so keep ours as well when rebuilding the station.
+	 */
+	bool ps = test_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &msta->wcid.flags);
 	int idx = 0;
 
 	memset(msta, 0, sizeof(*msta));
+	if (ps)
+		set_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &msta->wcid.flags);
 
 	idx = mt76_wcid_alloc(dev->mt76.wcid_mask, MT76x02_N_WCIDS);
 	if (idx < 0)
@@ -260,6 +266,12 @@
 	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
 		set_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_CHECK_PS, &msta->wcid.flags);
 
+	/* As mt76x02_sta_ps() left it; USB does not use the drop bit for
+	 * power save.
+	 */
+	if (ps && mt76_is_mmio(mdev))
+		mt76x02_mac_wcid_set_drop(dev, idx, true);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76x02_sta_add);
